1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,870
In December 1944 American generals had to prove that they were American,

2
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:10,270
because German soldiers in American uniforms were driving behind their lines.

3
00:00:10,360 --> 00:00:12,630
The plan was called Operation Greif.

4
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:16,240
It was led by Otto Skorzeny, the SS officer

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:20,500
who a year earlier had freed Mussolini from captivity in the Abruzzo mountains.

6
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:26,430
For the Ardennes offensive he was to raise a unit that looked and spoke like Americans.

7
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:29,950
But far too few volunteers with good English came forward,

8
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:37,410
and instead of hundreds of American vehicles Skorzeny got only a few jeeps, trucks and a single Sherman.

9
00:00:37,430 --> 00:00:40,450
The other tanks were disguised with sheet metal and paint.

10
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:43,050
On 16 December the offensive began.

11
00:00:43,070 --> 00:00:46,470
Small commando teams in captured jeeps turned signposts around,

12
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:50,530
cut telephone lines and sent columns the wrong way.

13
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:52,330
Only a few teams got through,

14
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:55,370
but the rumour spread faster than they did.

15
00:00:55,390 --> 00:00:59,190
At every crossroads American sentries now asked trick questions:

16
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:00,700
Who plays for the Yankees?

17
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:02,730
What is the name of Mickey Mouse's girlfriend?

18
00:01:02,810 --> 00:01:06,730
General Omar Bradley was asked for the capital of Illinois.

19
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:12,190
Captured commandos claimed that a team was on its way to Paris to kill Eisenhower.

20
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:13,420
There is no evidence for it,

21
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:17,820
yet the Supreme Commander spent Christmas under heavy guard.

22
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:20,680
Three men were stopped in a jeep near Aywaille.

23
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:22,410
They did not know the password,

24
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:25,180
a military court sentenced them as spies,

25
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,600
and before Christmas they were shot.

26
00:01:27,650 --> 00:01:33,450
Skorzeny himself stood trial in Dachau in 1947 and was acquitted.
